## Original hardware notes

The upstream project uses a resistor-based VGA output and a PIO-driven scanout path. The RCA 4:3 fork keeps the same framebuffer logic but moves the target to a simpler composite-friendly display mode.

## Firmware flash steps

```bash
# hold BOOTSEL on Pico
# drag and drop the generated UF2
```

After flashing:

- connect USB keyboard or mouse
- power the Pico from 5V
- connect RCA display and confirm the centered 4:3 frame appears
- if needed, adjust the resistor value from 220R to 470R for brightness/contrast

